## FEATURE B: Waitlist Email Notifications (Tier 2.3)

When a merchant has waiting customers for a ZIP, they should notify them with one click.

### Step 1: Read `app/routes/app.waitlist.tsx` COMPLETELY

Understand the current structure: how entries are listed, what action intents exist, what fetcher pattern is used.

### Step 2: Add `notify-zip` action intent

Add to the action function (before the final return):
```typescript
if (intent === "notify-zip") {
  const zipCode = String(formData.get("zipCode") || "").trim();
  if (!zipCode) return json({ error: "No ZIP code specified." });

  const entries = await db.waitlistEntry.findMany({
    where: { shop, zipCode, status: "waiting" },
    select: { id: true, email: true },
  });

  if (entries.length === 0) {
    return json({ action: "notify-zip", zipCode, emails: [], count: 0, message: "No waiting customers for this ZIP code." });
  }

  // Mark all as notified
  await db.waitlistEntry.updateMany({
    where: { shop, zipCode, status: "waiting" },
    data: { status: "notified" },
  });

  const emails = entries.map((e) => e.email);
  return json({ action: "notify-zip", zipCode, emails, count: emails.length });
}
```

### Step 3: Add state and effect

```typescript
const [notifyModalOpen, setNotifyModalOpen] = useState(false);
const [notifyData, setNotifyData] = useState<{ zipCode: string; emails: string[]; count: number } | null>(null);
const [copySuccess, setCopySuccess] = useState(false);
```

Add a useEffect after existing ones:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const d = fetcher.data as Record<string, unknown> | null | undefined;
  if (d && d.action === "notify-zip" && fetcher.state === "idle") {
    setNotifyData({
      zipCode: d.zipCode as string,
      emails: d.emails as string[],
      count: d.count as number,
    });
    setNotifyModalOpen(true);
  }
}, [fetcher.data, fetcher.state]);
```

### Step 4: Add "Notify Waiting Customers" UI

The waitlist page likely shows entries in a table. Add a "Notify" section above or inside the table. Find where unique ZIP codes are shown/calculated. Add a simple inline action for each unique ZIP that has "waiting" entries.

If the page has a stats section at the top (with counts like "Total: X, Waiting: Y"), add a "Notify by ZIP" card below it:

```tsx
{/* ZIP Notification Panel */}
<Card>
  <BlockStack gap="300">
    <Text as="h2" variant="headingSm">Notify Waiting Customers</Text>
    <Text as="p" variant="bodyMd" tone="subdued">
      Select a ZIP code to notify all waiting customers that delivery is now available.
    </Text>
    <InlineStack gap="300" align="start">
      <div style={{ minWidth: "200px" }}>
        <Select
          label="Select ZIP code"
          labelHidden
          options={[
            { label: "Select a ZIP code…", value: "" },
            ...waitingZips.map((z) => ({ label: `${z.zipCode} (${z.count} waiting)`, value: z.zipCode })),
          ]}
          value={selectedNotifyZip}
          onChange={setSelectedNotifyZip}
        />
      </div>
      <Button
        variant="primary"
        disabled={!selectedNotifyZip || isNotifying}
        loading={isNotifying}
        onClick={() => {
          const fd = new FormData();
          fd.set("intent", "notify-zip");
          fd.set("zipCode", selectedNotifyZip);
          fetcher.submit(fd, { method: "POST" });
        }}
      >
        Notify Waiting Customers
      </Button>
    </InlineStack>
  </BlockStack>
</Card>
```

Where `waitingZips` is derived from the loaded entries (computed from loader data):
```typescript
const waitingZips = useMemo(() => {
  const map = new Map<string, number>();
  (entries || []).forEach((e: { zipCode: string; status: string }) => {
    if (e.status === "waiting") {
      map.set(e.zipCode, (map.get(e.zipCode) || 0) + 1);
    }
  });
  return Array.from(map.entries()).map(([zipCode, count]) => ({ zipCode, count }));
}, [entries]);
```

And:
```typescript
const [selectedNotifyZip, setSelectedNotifyZip] = useState("");
const isNotifying = fetcher.state !== "idle" && fetcher.formData?.get("intent") === "notify-zip";
```

### Step 5: Add the notification result modal

```tsx
<Modal
  open={notifyModalOpen}
  onClose={() => { setNotifyModalOpen(false); setNotifyData(null); setCopySuccess(false); setSelectedNotifyZip(""); }}
  title={`Notify Waitlist — ZIP ${notifyData?.zipCode ?? ""}`}
  primaryAction={{
    content: "Done",
    onAction: () => { setNotifyModalOpen(false); setNotifyData(null); setCopySuccess(false); setSelectedNotifyZip(""); },
  }}
>
  <Modal.Section>
    <BlockStack gap="400">
      {notifyData && notifyData.count > 0 ? (
        <>
          <Banner tone="success">
            <Text as="p">
              <strong>{notifyData.count}</strong> customer{notifyData.count !== 1 ? "s" : ""} marked as notified for ZIP <strong>{notifyData.zipCode}</strong>.
            </Text>
          </Banner>
          <Text as="p" variant="bodyMd">
            Use the emails below to send your notification. Open in your email client or copy the list.
          </Text>
          <TextField
            label="Customer emails"
            value={notifyData.emails.join(", ")}
            onChange={() => {}}
            multiline={4}
            readOnly
            autoComplete="off"
          />
          <InlineStack gap="300">
            <Button
              onClick={() => {
                navigator.clipboard.writeText(notifyData.emails.join(", "));
                setCopySuccess(true);
                setTimeout(() => setCopySuccess(false), 2000);
              }}
            >
              {copySuccess ? "Copied!" : "Copy emails"}
            </Button>
            <Button
              url={`mailto:${notifyData.emails.join(",")}?subject=Great news! We now deliver to ZIP ${notifyData.zipCode}&body=Hi there!%0A%0AWe're excited to let you know that we now deliver to ZIP code ${notifyData.zipCode}.%0A%0AVisit our store to place your order!`}
              external
            >
              Open in email client
            </Button>
          </InlineStack>
        </>
      ) : (
        <Banner tone="info">
          <Text as="p">No waiting customers found for this ZIP code.</Text>
        </Banner>
      )}
    </BlockStack>
  </Modal.Section>
</Modal>
```

